.TH CREATE\-REPORT\-PTS 1 "February 2026" "benchmarking" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
create\-report\-pts.sh \- generate PTS reports from benchmark results
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B create\-report\-pts.sh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fIrun\-dir\fR
[\fIrun\-dir\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates reports in all supported PTS export formats from
.B benchmark\-results/
directories produced by any of the benchmark scripts
(\fBbenchmark\-cpu\-pts.sh\fR, \fBbenchmark\-memory\-pts.sh\fR,
\fBbenchmark\-network\-pts.sh\fR, \fBbenchmark\-storage\-pts.sh\fR).
.PP
PTS result directories are detected automatically by locating
.B composite.xml
files inside each supplied run directory.
Results are grouped by test type (PTS identifier with version suffix stripped,
e.g.\& all
.I pts/fio\-*
variants group under
.IR pts/fio ).
When more than one run directory is supplied and the same test type is found in
multiple runs, the results are merged using
.B phoronix\-test\-suite merge\-results
for side-by-side comparison.
A single run directory is also supported; in that case all test types found are
exported individually without merging.
.PP
All temporary PTS result entries imported during processing are removed on exit.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.TP
.B text
Human-readable summary table.
File extension:
.BR .text .
.TP
.B csv
Flat CSV suitable for spreadsheet import.
File extension:
.BR .csv .
.TP
.B json
Structured JSON for custom processing or automation.
File extension:
.BR .json .
.TP
.B html
Self-contained HTML page with charts.
File extension:
.BR .html .
.TP
.B pdf
PDF report.
Requires
.BR wkhtmltopdf (1)
to be installed.
File extension:
.BR .pdf .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Directory to write reports into.
Default:
.BR ./pts\-reports/<timestamp>/ .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help message and exit.
.SH RESULT NAMING
The \fB\-\-result\-id\fR value supplied to a benchmark script controls the run
directory name and, for CPU/memory/network scripts, the prefix of each PTS
result subdirectory inside it.
For the storage script the disk label (from \fB\-\-disk\fR) names the PTS result
subdirectories within a run.
.PP
.TS
lb lb lb
l l l.
Script	PTS result subdirectory name	Differentiator
benchmark\-cpu\-pts.sh	<result\-id>	\-\-result\-id
benchmark\-memory\-pts.sh	<result\-id>_<test>	\-\-result\-id
benchmark\-network\-pts.sh	<result\-id>_<test\-variant>	\-\-result\-id
benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh	<disk\-label>_<test>_result	disk label in \-\-disk
.TE
.SH OUTPUT
Reports are written under
.IR output\-dir ,
organised by test type:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pts\-reports/<timestamp>/
  pts\-fio/
    pts\-fio.text
    pts\-fio.csv
    pts\-fio.json
    pts\-fio.html
    pts\-fio.pdf
  pts\-stream/
    \&...
.RE
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Generate reports for a single memory benchmark run:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./create\-report\-pts.sh ./benchmark\-results/dc1\-node3\-ddr5/
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compare two memory runs (baseline vs tuned):
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-memory\-pts.sh \-\-result\-id "node3\-baseline"
\&./benchmark\-memory\-pts.sh \-\-result\-id "node3\-tuned"
\&./create\-report\-pts.sh \\
    ./benchmark\-results/node3\-baseline/ \\
    ./benchmark\-results/node3\-tuned/
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compare two disk types from a single storage run:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh \\
    \-\-disk "/dev/vdb;NVMe" \\
    \-\-disk "/dev/vdc;HDD" \\
    \-\-result\-id "storage\-q1\-2026"
\&./create\-report\-pts.sh ./benchmark\-results/storage\-q1\-2026/
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compare the same disk type across two storage runs with a custom output path:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./create\-report\-pts.sh \\
    \-\-output\-dir /tmp/storage\-comparison \\
    ./benchmark\-results/before\-upgrade/ \\
    ./benchmark\-results/after\-upgrade/
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR benchmark\-cpu\-pts.sh (1),
.BR benchmark\-memory\-pts.sh (1),
.BR benchmark\-network\-pts.sh (1),
.BR benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh (1),
.BR phoronix\-test\-suite (1)
